## 'loop' needs a body. Unlike while and until it takes no condition, so the
## body is the only thing it can be missing.
##
## [NOTE] only a MISSING body is refused. A bare expression is accepted as one
## - "loop (+ 1 2)" compiles and then spins forever - so there is no error
## case to assert for that shape, and writing one here hangs the suite.

loop;  ##ERROR: syntax error - no loop body specified in loop

---

## break belongs to a loop

break;  ##ERROR: syntax error - break outside loop

---

## and so does continue

continue;  ##ERROR: syntax error - continue outside loop
